## R2 — CoVIA+ / CoOrb+ channel evolution

Candidate interpretation:

`CoVIA+` = **conversation/input/output relational channel fabric**, not one chat tab.

It should bind:
`participant | intent | draft/commit state | source time | observation time | receiver | modality | privacy | authority | currentness | payload | projection | response | receipt | successor`

This makes the present conversation only one embodiment of CoVIA+, alongside local voice, text, CoOrb, CoBar/RickBar, mobile, headset, email-like surfaces, machine twins and future substrates.

### CoOrb+ as ambient embodiment

CoOrb+ can be the low-attention, persistent projection of CoVIA+ and related CoAll state:

- currentness / liveness;
- active front / task;
- draft vs committed intent;
- prediction confidence;
- attention / pressure;
- receiver readiness;
- exception / recovery state;
- CoTime/read cursor;
- quick expand into CoPop/CoPanel/CoMap;
- handoff between modalities/substrates.

`COVIA_NE_CHAT_TAB`
`COORB_NE_CONTROL_PLANE`
`AMBIENT_NE_AUTHORITATIVE`
`VISIBLE_NE_CURRENT_UNLESS_RECEIPTED`

### Temporal input relation

For typing/voice/gesture where an actual receiver exists:

`RAW_INPUT -> DRAFT_SIGNAL -> INTENT_CANDIDATE -> COMMIT -> QUALIFIED_INTENT -> BOUNDED_ACTION_CANDIDATE -> AUTH_CHECK -> DEED -> RECEIPT -> FEEDBACK`

Draft signals may drive reversible prediction/prefetch/render preparation, but never silently become effect authority.

`DRAFT_NE_COMMIT`
`PREDICTION_NE_INTENT`
`INPUT_NE_AUTHORITY`

### Channel continuity

CoVIA+ should survive embodiment changes:

`chat -> CoOrb -> voice -> mobile -> XR -> CoBar -> machine twin`

while preserving:
- conversation/thread identity where useful;
- read cursor;
- provenance;
- unsent draft boundaries;
- privacy/authority;
- currentness;
- delivery/pickup distinction;
- supersession/handoff state.

`CHANNEL_CHANGE_NE_CONTEXT_ERASURE`
`DELIVERY_NE_PICKUP`
`HANDOFF_NE_AUTHORITY_TRANSFER`

### Feedback / AutoEvo

Every CoVIA/CoOrb interaction can feed:
`response latency | comprehension | correction | challenge | dismiss/snooze/pin | follow-through | stale detection | recovery | task completion`

into CoAckRewised / AutoEvo calibration, provided private/sensitive input is handled under explicit retention/privacy rules.

`FEEDBACK_NE_SURVEILLANCE`
`INTERACTION_NE_CONSENT_TO_RETAIN_FOREVER`

### CoOrb projection family

A useful CoOrb may have states:
`QUIET | GLANCE | LISTENING | DRAFTING | THINKING | WAITING | READY | WARNING | RECOVERY | HUMAN_GATE | SLEEP`

with visual motion/color/size as projections only, never proof.

`ANIMATION_NE_LIVENESS`
`ORB_STATE_NE_RUNTIME_STATE_UNLESS_RECEIPTED`

### Multi-orb / swarm relation

Multiple orbs may represent distinct fronts/models/devices/participants, but the default should remain compressed and exception-first.

`MULTI_ORB_NE_MULTI_CONTROL_PLANE`
`ORB_COUNT_NE_WORKER_COUNT`
`MANY_LOGICAL_ORBS_NE_MANY_MATERIAL_PROCESSES`

### CoVIA+ next bounded proof

1. define a machine-readable `CoVIAChannel.R0` object;
2. bind one live local CoOrb instance to exact observed currentness + read cursor;
3. distinguish draft/commit/receipt states visibly;
4. canary one modality handoff with no context loss;
5. measure human time-to-orientation and false-alert rate;
6. only then broaden persistence/startup/default surface use.

No claim here that CoVIA+ already exists as a runtime fabric or that current CoOrb is globally bound to this contract.
